  195 => [
    'transcript' => 'The elaborate paintings found in caves such as Lascaux and Chauvet, depicting horses, bison, and other Ice Age fauna with remarkable anatomical accuracy, represent some of the earliest unambiguous evidence of symbolic thought in our species. These images were often painted deep within cave systems, far from any evidence of habitation, requiring artificial lighting and considerable effort to access. This suggests the act of creating and viewing these images carried ritual or spiritual significance rather than serving a purely decorative function tied to daily living space. Such findings have led researchers to regard these painted caves as evidence of complex cognitive and ...',
