    'transcript' => 'Buildings account for a substantial share of global energy consumption, largely due to heating, cooling, and lighting systems that often operate inefficiently in older structures. Green building certification programs, such as LEED, establish rigorous standards for insulation, window design, and mechanical systems that collectively reduce a building\'s energy demand. Structures designed according to these standards frequently incorporate features such as high-efficiency HVAC systems, natural daylighting, and smart thermostats that adjust automatically based on occupancy. Property developers who invest in these upgrades typically recoup their initial costs within a few years through significant reductions in ...',
