  266 => [
    'transcript' => 'Once individuals purchase comprehensive insurance coverage that shields them from the financial consequences of risky behavior, their incentive to exercise caution can diminish. A driver who knows that any accident-related repair costs will be fully covered by their insurer, for instance, might drive somewhat less carefully than someone bearing the full cost of a potential collision personally. Insurers have long recognized this behavioral shift and attempt to counteract it through deductibles and premium adjustments. This tendency for insured individuals to take on greater risk precisely because they are shielded from its consequences is known as ...',
