    'transcript' => 'Residents of rural and remote regions frequently face significant barriers to receiving specialized medical care, since many specialists concentrate their practices in urban centers where patient volumes are higher. Traveling several hours to see a cardiologist or dermatologist is often impractical for patients who lack reliable transportation or cannot take extended time away from work. Telemedicine platforms address this gap by allowing patients to consult with specialists remotely through video calls, eliminating the need for lengthy travel in many routine cases. Health policy researchers have found that expanding telemedicine services in underserved areas substantially improves ...',
